      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={4}^{x}\\log _{4} (x),$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=4^{x} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={4}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\log _{4} (x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & ={({4}^{x})}^{\u2032}\\log _{4} (x)+{4}^{x}{(\\log _{4} (x))}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =({4}^{x}\\ln  (4))(\\log _{4} (x))+({4}^{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\ln  (4)}) \\\\  & ={4}^{x}\\ln  (4)\\log _{4} (x)+\\frac{{4}^{x}}{x\\ln  (4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
